id: pm-bzmeaa
title: "Strategic reachability invariant: every active item resolves to an outcome milestone through a typed, explainable path within a bounded hop count"
description: ""
type: Task
status: open
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:sdk",context-management,depth,governance,graph,relationships,traceability
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:47:30.529Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T23:47:30.529Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 1500
acceptance_criteria: "The audit profile reports depth distribution, eccentricity, and shortest-path-to-milestone for every active item, not just isolate and degree counts; A declared policy states the maximum acceptable hop distance to an outcome milestone and the minimum distinct edge-kind count on the path; Violations surface as audit findings with a remediation hint naming candidate anchors, never as an instruction to fabricate an edge; Deliberately shallow items are representable as reviewed waivers with recorded rationale rather than silently failing; The profile is computed within the graph analytics token and latency budgets and stays bounded at million-item scale"
goal: explainable-graph
objective: Graph algorithms alone can answer why any item exists and which outcome it serves
value: "The graph currently guarantees that no active item is isolated. That is a floor, not a structure: an item can satisfy it with one parent edge and still be unreachable from any strategic outcome, which means no traversal can explain why it is being worked on."
impact: "Turns the relationship graph from a connectivity artifact into a navigable explanation of the project, which is the precondition for graph-driven context assembly and for the reachability-based relevance signals the context engine wants."
outcome: "A governance profile reports, for every active item, the shortest typed path to an outcome milestone and the edge-kind diversity along it; violations are findings with named owners."
why_now: "Outcome milestones now exist as graph roots, so reachability finally has a defined target. Measuring depth before the terminal-history backfill waves run means the waves can be aimed at the actual gaps."
parent: pm-96h7
risk: medium
confidence: medium
